  "term": "ambiguity scale",
  "definition": "An ambiguity scale is a questionnaire measure used to assess tolerance of ambiguity, meaning how much a person can handle unclear or uncertain situations. In this study context, it was used as a personality-related measure linked to how people respond when their expectations are contradicted.",
